      "message": "As far as I can tell, the dma_buf heap allocation mechanism doesn\u0027t support creating read-only files. However now that you point it out, if some driver produces them by directly calling `dma_buf_fd`, you\u0027re right that they could set read-only flags on it.\n\nOn the other hand, such permissions (or the lack of a read permission) might also be placed on secure memory which needs to be donated. I\u0027ll handle that in a separate path though when it\u0027s added.\n\nI\u0027ve restored _RO functionality.",
